From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 12:05:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rhodep: give the display its interconnect
 paths

The mdss node has no interconnects property, so
msm_mdss_parse_data_bus_icc_path() gets NULL from devm_of_icc_get() and
leaves num_mdp_paths at 0. Every icc_set_bw() in msm_mdss.c then iterates
over an empty array and the reg bus path is NULL, so the display driver
runs without ever asking for a single byte of bandwidth. The perf figures
the DPU catalog carries for this SoC -- min_dram_ib = 1600000,
min_core_ib = 2500000 in sm6375_perf_data -- are computed and thrown away.

This shows up as DSI HS FIFO underflow. With a diagnostic patch printing
the raw error registers, every single occurrence reads:

  fifo=88881010 timeout=00000001 ack=00000000 status0=00000005
  phy=00088888 clk=008037c3 mdp_busy=1 dma_busy=0

DLN0..3_HS_FIFO_UNDERFLOW on all four lanes, with the MDP mid-transfer
and the command DMA idle. The link is starved, not contended: pclk0 is
63887989 Hz and carries 3 bytes per cycle without widebus, which is
191.66 MB/s, and byte0_clk is 47915991 Hz across 4 lanes, which is the
same 191.66 MB/s. Supply equals demand exactly, by construction, so the
lane FIFOs only ever hold jitter. Any stall in the DPU's fetch drains
them, and with no bandwidth vote the fetch is at the mercy of whatever
else is using DDR.

It reproduces accordingly: 0 errors on an idle screen, 0 under a pure
memory load with the screen static, 0 driving the backlight 120 times
with the screen static, and errors only when something repaints -- worst
while several applications start at once, which is also when the port
stutters.

Use the same paths sm6115 uses, that being the closest SMD-RPM sibling.

The provider has to be built in rather than modular for this. Once the
mdss node names an interconnect, its probe defers until the provider
registers, and the provider is a module that userspace has kept
blacklisted since kali-boot-v96. Loading it by hand on this device tree
binds all six buses cleanly -- snoc, the clk/mmrt/mmnrt virtuals, cnoc
and bimc -- so the blacklist has outlived the bug it was written for
(fixed in 0027), but a display that cannot come up without a module is
not a trade worth making.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -1054,6 +1054,13 @@
 
 		iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x820 0x2>;
 
+		interconnects = <&mmrt_virt MASTER_MDP_PORT0 RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+				 &bimc SLAVE_EBI RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>,
+				<&bimc MASTER_AMPSS_M0 RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+				 &config_noc SLAVE_DISPLAY_CFG RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>;
+		interconnect-names = "mdp0-mem",
+				     "cpu-cfg";
+
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
